From a0851fd3bb0226200822220738713005106f1ce7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Remora <remora@localhost>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 09:55:23 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] A17 LineageOS SDK: Trust warnings are off until the user
 turns them on

TrustInterfaceService checks two things at every boot once the user has
been through the Trust onboarding: that SELinux is enforcing and that
the build is not signed with test keys. Each failure posts a
high-importance notification. In a container both fail by construction:
there is no SELinux (Trust reports it Disabled), and the image is a
test-keys build. With trust_warnings unset, which the upstream code
treats as every warning on, each boot would post two security warnings
that nothing on the device can resolve.

Unset now means no warnings. The Trust screen still shows the SELinux,
security patch and encryption status, and its Alerts switches still
turn either warning on. LineageParts' TrustPreferences reads the same
default (its own patch), so those switches show what the service does.

Change-Id: I946d99e4ca6e750257f20093daa2bef8d528a49b
---
 .../lineageos/platform/internal/TrustInterfaceService.java | 7 +++++--
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/lineage/lib/main/java/org/lineageos/platform/internal/TrustInterfaceService.java b/lineage/lib/main/java/org/lineageos/platform/internal/TrustInterfaceService.java
index 97d684ac..3f1363fd 100644
--- a/lineage/lib/main/java/org/lineageos/platform/internal/TrustInterfaceService.java
+++ b/lineage/lib/main/java/org/lineageos/platform/internal/TrustInterfaceService.java
@@ -217,10 +217,13 @@ public class TrustInterfaceService extends LineageSystemService {
         return mContext.getPackageManager().hasSystemFeature(PackageManager.FEATURE_LEANBACK);
     }
 
+    // Remora: off until the user turns a warning on. Both checks fail by construction in a
+    // container (there is no SELinux, and the image is signed with test keys), so the upstream
+    // default posted two warnings on every boot that nothing could resolve. LineageParts'
+    // TrustPreferences reads the same default.
     private boolean isWarningAllowed(int warning) {
         return (LineageSettings.Secure.getInt(mContext.getContentResolver(),
-                LineageSettings.Secure.TRUST_WARNINGS,
-                TrustInterface.TRUST_WARN_MAX_VALUE) & warning) != 0;
+                LineageSettings.Secure.TRUST_WARNINGS, 0) & warning) != 0;
     }
 
     private Pair<Integer, Integer> getNotificationStringsForFeature(int feature) {
-- 
